   "subject": "Clarification on 'first-available' resource selection",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">I was wondering if you could please clarify how the &#39;first-available&#39; selection policy works, specifically in terms of what conditions are checked to determine &quot;first-available&quot;. </span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">Does this look only at the resource capacity schedule (i.e., the first resource to have capacity &gt;0) or does it also look at which resource will first have queue count = 0? How does the selection work if multiple resources are provided that are tied for capacity, server, and queue counts? </span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">Thank you.</span></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bFh9QlohCQAJ",
   "from": "Iñaki Ucar",
   "author": "0f5b7adb7e70bd8b",
   "date": "2023-05-30T19:44:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: [simmer-devel] Clarification on 'first-available' resource selection",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first-available policy checks the resources in the order given, and selects the first one with a server count that is less than the capacity. If all resources are busy, then it selects the first one with space in the queue. You can check the logic <a href=\"https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/blob/cb9b0651d1c7b6fa364fee708407ec6b4619a2d3/inst/include/simmer/activity/resource_internal.h#L132\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/blob/cb9b0651d1c7b6fa364fee708407ec6b4619a2d3/inst/include/simmer/activity/resource_internal.h%23L132&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467252599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3W1Q17QtsAttDAn9cq2Hzp\">here</a>. <div><br></div><div>Iñaki</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, 30 May 2023 at 16:32, Philemon Cyclone &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">phil.m.f...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">I was wondering if you could please clarify how the &#39;first-available&#39; selection policy works, specifically in terms of what conditions are checked to determine &quot;first-available&quot;. </span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">Does this look only at the resource capacity schedule (i.e., the first resource to have capacity &gt;0) or does it also look at which resource will first have queue count = 0? How does the selection work if multiple resources are provided that are tied for capacity, server, and queue counts? </span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&